CUDA: GGML_CUDA_MMQ_FEW=0 turns off the few-row MMQ kernel

llama.cpp 1.0 (#31533) gives quantized products of 2 to 24 tokens an int8 MMA kernel of
its own, from 3 or 4 columns on depending on the type (tuned on an RTX 5090). With --mtp 2 the
check of the drafts is a product of 3 tokens: on the reference PC (RTX 5070 Ti, Qwen3.5-9B Q4_K_M)
v1.0.0 kept 61% of the drafts against 68% for b12283 and wrote 4-7% slower. GGML_CUDA_MMQ_FEW=0
sends those products back to MMVQ and MMQ, to tell whether this kernel or another change of the
release is the cause, and to keep the old path where it measures better. Read once.

EuLLM patch on llama.cpp v1.0.0 (b12359).

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmq-few.cu b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmq-few.cu
